    /// Live aircraft positions in a map view (adsb.lol), a separate layer from events.
    ///
    /// Positions are cached in memory and never stored. The world is cut into 5° cells (on multiples of 5°); `bbox` is required and may span at most 4 of them, else 400 ("zoom in"): a view up to 5° high and 5° wide always fits, up to 10° × 10° fits when aligned. Each cell is refreshed from the feed at most once a minute, and only while its daily quota allows. Without a key (500 requests a day) the whole server gets one request every ~3 minutes, so one viewer's 4-cell view is up to 12 minutes old: show `dataAt`, and poll no faster than once a minute. A cell with no data younger than 15 minutes is left out and `complete` is false. Aircraft whose operators opted out of display (FAA LADD, privacy ICAO addresses) are never returned. Military aircraft are returned as the feed reports them, with `military` set. Data ODbL 1.0: show `attribution` on the map.
